        "en": "Before the mystery of death, problematic man discovers his true calling. Death is by no means the brutal annihilation of consciousness, but the eschatological transition wherein love bears witness to its sovereign immortality. This spiritual victory over the vertigo of doubt attests the indestructible fecundity of invocation and grace (Part II, §90)."
